<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Thank you. I wanted to drop the power down a bit, but instead of dropping the setting to 3800, I changed the power setting to 4 watts GARY</div></blockquote>The setting you described is only for the Custom power setting. It allows you to set the PA drive from no drive at all to the maximum the hardware is capable of.<br><br>Note.  The maximum setting should be used with caution be because it can cause overheating of the PA FET.<br><br>If you want to change the power output, you should normally use the normal power controls,  e.g 1 to 5w etc<br><br>If your radio is not outputting the correct power eg not 5w on the 5w setting you need to use the calibration functionality<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sun Mar 23, 2025 3:33 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
